## ⚠️ 5. The Most Critical Aspect: Stop-Loss Strategy
Earnings volatility can be extreme. Without a stop-loss, minor losses can escalate into major drawdowns.

### 1. Define Maximum Acceptable Loss
Decide pre-trade: "What is the maximum I am willing to lose on this trade?"
(E.g., limit single-trade loss to 2%–5% of total capital).

### 2. Avoid Emotional Bias
Resist thoughts like "It's a good company, it will bounce back." Post-earnings, the market may reprice based on new data. Short-term price action can diverge from long-term fundamentals.

### 3. Avoid Going All-In
Single-day swings during earnings can be violent. Full exposure amplifies emotional decision-making under pressure.

